  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U10U-READ-1",
      "title": "International Night",
      "text": "Our school held an international night last Friday. Along with students from Japan and Vietnam, our class cooked a balanced meal of rice, meat, and vegetables. At first I was too shy to utter a word, but I soon made friends with two exchange students. They asked me about the cultural meaning of moon cakes, and I did my best to express the idea in English. One student took photos of every dish, so I asked him for a favor: to send them to our class group. In our haste to clean up, we almost had an accident with a pot of hot soup. Luckily nobody got hurt, and we did not waste any food. Our teacher said our class got along with the guests better than average."
    }
  ],
